// A DIAGNOSTIC config. Nothing runs it automatically, and it does NOT pass.
//
// `tsconfig.json` here has `include: ["src"]`, so neither `tsc -b` nor vitest
// ever typechecks `test/**`. A type error in a new test file is therefore
// INVISIBLE to CI — the test still runs, because vitest transpiles without
// checking, so the file goes green while lying about the types it asserts on.
// Two real errors in `test/facade/status-category.test.ts` were found exactly
// this way and fixed before that file was committed (a missing `EntityRelations`
// field, and an unguarded regex capture).
//
//     npx tsc -p packages/server/tsconfig.tests.json
//
// As of 2026-08-18 that reports 216 PRE-EXISTING errors across 39 test files,
// which is why this is not wired into `tools/ci/check.sh`: turning it on is a
// cleanup of its own, not a rider on a feature branch. Until someone does that,
// the way to use this is to run it and grep for YOUR file.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "incremental": false,
    "rootDir": "."
  },
  "include": ["src", "test"]
}
